# Folder library

Canonical brief: [`.cursor/saved/folder-library/BRIEF.md`](../saved/folder-library/BRIEF.md)  
Gallery/table ref (strip only): [`.cursor/saved/folder-library/LibraryTable.gallery.original.tsx`](../saved/folder-library/LibraryTable.gallery.original.tsx)  
FileCard ref: [`.cursor/saved/folder-library/FileCard.original.tsx`](../saved/folder-library/FileCard.original.tsx)

## Product

- **Folder-scoped** library first (no workspace UI yet).
- Goal: **fancy recall + visualization** (tips, trailer, download) — not dump storage.
- Ficha = tag + tips + optional **attachment** + optional **preview** (images / trailer ≤~1 min). Almost everything optional.
- **Library table (folder):** `[+]` + **type tabs** (Image / PDF / Skill / Auto) + thumb grid. **No “All” in v1** — one type at a time; `[+]` uses current type; name = ficha tag.
- **Document (later):** minimal FileCard-style strip — not the full folder table.
- **Atelier:** open image/trailer space → wall background color + **social hex**; human craft, FN does not generate images.
- Bytes → Supabase **`doc-images`**. Metadatos → `campaigns.library_items` jsonb.

## Gina

Library data is **live corpus for Gina**. She should **remember and show** fichas in the **same chat during the day**. Do not build library-only silos Gina cannot read. LIVE CORPUS ONLY — never invent files.

## Code today

- CRUD: `src/lib/folderLibrary.js` + normalize
- UI: `FolderLibraryOverlay` (type filter + grid) / `FolderLibraryElementModal`
- Persist: `campaigns.library_items` via `supabase_campaign_library_items.sql` + `persistenceMiddleware` upsert/hydrate
- Gap: atelier / doc mini strip / Gina library tools

## Do not

- Invent a second hierarchy instead of hanging on folder docs
- Drop Tailwind Magic into the app without adapting to FN CSS / `#151515`
- Port AI Multi-Modal generation (prompts, models, loaders, history, generate CTA)
- Assume AI image generation inside the atelier
- Mix all file types in one grid by default
- Put the full folder table inside open documents — docs get a small FileCard strip later
